# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEDCARE PRO — environment template.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
#
# This is a single shared deployment serving every tenant, so there is exactly
# one of each of these values — not one set per clinic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Database — the single shared Hostinger MySQL database (PRD §8).
DATABASE_URL="mysql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:3306/DATABASE_NAME"

# Auth.js — generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=""
# Public URL of the deployment.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email — required by FR-1.2 (signup verification links).
# Provider: Resend (implemented in src/lib/email.ts).
#
# EMAIL_API_KEY       Resend API key — starts with "re_".
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS  Sender on a domain verified in Resend, e.g.
#                     "MEDCARE PRO <noreply@yourdomain.com>". Resend rejects
#                     sends from unverified domains.
#
# The verification link's origin is taken from NEXTAUTH_URL above, so no
# separate app-URL variable is needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EMAIL_API_KEY=""
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp — provider: RkvRobo (https://bot.rkvrobo.in).
#
# NOT the Meta Cloud API and NOT an official BSP: RkvRobo drives real WhatsApp
# devices through its own portal. Two consequences worth knowing:
#
#   - There is no provider-side template approval. The approved message set
#     lives in this app (`whatsapp_templates`), and no endpoint here accepts a
#     free-typed body.
#   - There is no delivery-status callback. A send is known only as accepted or
#     rejected at the gateway — never as delivered or read. There is therefore
#     no webhook secret to configure.
#
# WHATSAPP_BSP_API_KEY       From the RkvRobo panel. Sending is disabled while
#                            this is blank; the Messages page says so.
# WHATSAPP_BSP_API_BASE_URL  Optional override. Defaults to
#                            https://bot.rkvrobo.in/api
# WHATSAPP_BSP_SENDER        Which connected device sends. Defaults to
#                            "rotate", which spreads sends across every
#                            Rotate-ON device in the panel — with more than one
#                            number connected that is the safer default, since
#                            it avoids concentrating traffic on a single one.
#                            Set a specific number to pin sends to one device.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHATSAPP_BSP_API_KEY=""
WHATSAPP_BSP_API_BASE_URL=""
WHATSAPP_BSP_SENDER="rotate"
